# Blank lines or lines beginning with a # are ignored.

# Name of your weblog. Placed in title tags.
name=My Weblog

# Absolute URL of your weblog, no trailing slash needed.
# Setting this turns on the RSS feed at /rss.xml. Leave it
# commented out and no feed is built.
#url=https://example.com

# markdown= overrides the processor `make setup` detected.
# It is a shell command line, run as: <command> <file>
# It must write an HTML *fragment* to stdout and exit
# non-zero on failure. Like deploy.sh, it is executed --
# only put something here you would run yourself.
#
# A # after markdown= does NOT start a comment: the whole
# rest of the line is part of the command, and the shell
# running it will treat the # as its own comment marker.
#
# These are the command lines `make setup` detects, in the
# order it prefers them. Uncommenting one pins that choice.
#
# markdown=lowdown --out-no-smarty --html-no-skiphtml --html-no-escapehtml
# markdown=cmark-gfm --unsafe -e table -e strikethrough -e autolink -e tasklist
# markdown=md2html --github
# markdown=comrak --unsafe -e table
# markdown=multimarkdown --snippet
# markdown=markdown -f +tables,-smarty
# markdown=cmark --unsafe
# markdown=smu
# markdown=markdown_py -x tables
# markdown=markdown-it --html
# markdown=pandoc -f markdown-smart -t html
